1
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:02,020
Oh, it's a quarter to four,

2
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:04,590
and I have a production meeting at four.

3
00:01:04,590 --> 00:01:06,970
I planned to take you for a ride in Central Park

4
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:08,910
in a horse and carriage.

5
00:01:08,910 --> 00:01:10,080
Harry, I'd love to,

6
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,490
but I have work to do.

7
00:01:12,490 --> 00:01:16,370
OK. We'll walk back to your office with you.

8
00:01:16,370 --> 00:01:18,480
It's so nice out.

9
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:20,970
I decided to forget about my accounting problems

10
00:01:20,970 --> 00:01:24,600
and just enjoy this beautiful spring day.

11
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:26,440
Take the time, Susan.

12
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:27,850
I know I should,

13
00:01:27,850 --> 00:01:32,380
but ... well, there are too many things to do.

14
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:33,440
I understand.

15
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:35,910
I'll go for a ride with Michelle.

16
00:01:35,910 --> 00:01:37,310
Right.

17
00:01:37,310 --> 00:01:41,690
Well, I had a really nice time.

18
00:01:41,690 --> 00:01:42,920
So did I.

19
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:44,330
So did I.

20
00:01:44,330 --> 00:01:46,760
I'm sorry you can't come with us, Susan.

21
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:48,880
So am I.

22
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:51,590
Bye-bye.

23
00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:59,860
Harry! Michelle! Can you wait till I make a phone call?

24
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:14,910
Sure.

25
00:02:14,910 --> 00:02:16,880
Susan Stewart's office.

26
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:18,350
Sam, this is Susan.

27
00:02:18,350 --> 00:02:19,720
Hi. How was lunch?

28
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:21,330
Fine.

29
00:02:21,330 --> 00:02:22,860
You're late.

30
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:25,490
The production department's waiting in the conference room.

31
00:02:25,490 --> 00:02:26,360
I know.

32
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,180
Ask Paul Smith to fill in for me.

33
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:29,640
He knows everything about the production schedule,

34
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:31,730
and he can answer any questions.

35
00:02:31,730 --> 00:02:32,980
Right.

36
00:02:32,980 --> 00:02:34,280
Don't tell any one,

37
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:37,370
but I'm taking a little time to smell the flowers.

38
00:02:37,370 --> 00:02:37,910
Good for you.

39
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:38,990
It'll be our secret.

40
00:02:38,990 --> 00:02:41,270
But schedule another production meeting for tomorrow.

41
00:02:41,270 --> 00:02:42,030
I'll be back

42
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:43,810
for my six o'clock appointment with Mr. Ozawa.

43
00:02:43,810 --> 00:02:44,500
OK, Susan.

44
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:46,050
And have a nice afternoon.

45
00:02:46,050 --> 00:03:28,740
Thanks.

46
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:29,830
She likes you.

47
00:03:29,830 --> 00:03:31,770
I know. I like her.

48
00:03:31,770 --> 00:03:32,850
How'd you do it?

49
00:03:32,850 --> 00:03:34,380
We had a talk.

50
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:35,640
About what?

51
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:37,310
Life.

52
00:03:37,310 --> 00:03:38,820
And what did you decide?

53
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:41,820
That's a secret ... between us women.
